{
 "encounter_id": "00974",
 "speakers": {
  "person_1": "PATIENT",
  "person_2": "DOCTOR",
  "person_3": "FAMILY_MEMBER"
 },
 "turns": [
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Mr Fenwick, Mrs Fenwick, come in. Is this about the gabapentin? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Er, yes. It's the, what do you call it, the tablets. The drowsy. I've been so sleepy I can't, er, I fell asleep in the garden, in the rain."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "He's nodding off all day, doctor. At the table, in front of the telly, in the car, I won't let him drive."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Since when?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Since they put the dose up last month."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Are you steady on your feet, Mr Fenwick?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "A bit wobbly. Like I've had a few."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "And your vision?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Blurry, now and then. Especially on the stairs."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Have you had any falls?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "No, thank goodness, but he's had a few near misses."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any confusion?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No, I'm not confused. Just sleepy."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any swelling in the ankles?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "No, they look the same."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any low mood?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No, I'm cheerful, if tired."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Remind me, what dose were you on, and what is it now?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "He was on 300 mg three times a day, then the pain clinic put it to 600 mg three times a day."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Thank you. Any allergies to medicines?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "None. No allergies."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Your history?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Nerve pain in his feet, from the diabetes. And the diabetes itself, type 2."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Operations?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "A hip replacement, in 2018."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Family history?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "My father had a stroke. My brother has diabetes."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "What did you do, Mr Fenwick?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Bus driver. Retired."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Do you drink?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "A pint on a Friday."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "And what do you do now to keep active?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "He plays bowls on Wednesdays, when he's awake."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Let me check you. Pulse 68, blood pressure 130 over 76, temperature 36.5, oxygen 97 percent, breathing 14, weight 83 kilos.",
   "pause": 15.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Is that all right? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "All fine. Mr Fenwick, walk to the door and back for me.",
   "pause": 10.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I'll try. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "You're steady but slow, and you veer slightly to the left."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "He does that. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Let me tap your ankles. The reflexes at the ankles are reduced."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "That's the diabetes. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "And the feeling in your feet is reduced to light touch."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Yes, they're numb. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "And there's no swelling in the ankles."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Good. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any trouble with your breathing?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No, nothing like that."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Here's what I think. The drowsiness and unsteadiness fit the higher dose of gabapentin. I think the dose is too high for you."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Can he just stop it? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "No, stopping suddenly isn't safe. I'd like to reduce the gabapentin to 300 mg, three times a day."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Will the pain come back? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Possibly a little. That's why we'll go step by step. I'd also like to arrange blood tests, including kidney function, since gabapentin is cleared by the kidneys."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Is it his kidneys? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Unlikely, but worth checking. I'd also like an HbA1c, and a vitamin B12 level, since these can cause nerve problems."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Fine. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Please don't drive until the sleepiness has settled."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "He won't. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "If the drowsiness doesn't improve in two weeks, come back and see me."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Two weeks. We'll watch him. ~"
  }
 ],
